        "original_id": "2d9e0fe2-6133-5e72-acf8-e802bb386268",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Frideric Handel\n- Products: Keyboard glockenspiel; Keyboard suite in D minor (HWV 437)\n- Works: Saul\n- Topics: Handel's musical influences\n\nFacts:\n- George Frideric Handel composed the Keyboard suite in D minor (HWV 437) for solo keyboard, specifically harpsichord, between 1703 and 1706.\n- In 1739, the keyboard glockenspiel was first used by George Frideric Handel in the oratorio Saul.\n- George Frideric Handel was strongly influenced by the great composers of the Italian Baroque and by the middle-German polyphonic choral tradition.",
